{%- set owner = slug | split(pat="/") | first -%}
{%- set first = variants.0 -%}
{%- set mirror = theme.id ~ "-starship" -%}
# {{ theme.name }} Starship Theme

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This repository is a read-only mirror.
> Issues, pull requests, and stars should go to [{{ slug }}]({{ theme.repository }}).

Starship prompt themes for {{ theme.name }}. {{ theme.description }}

## Installation

Clone the repository and add the palette to your Starship config:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/{{ owner }}/{{ mirror }}.git
cat {{ mirror }}/{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}.toml >> ~/.config/starship.toml
```

Then set the palette in your config:

```toml
palette = '{{ theme.id }}-{{ first.variant.id }}'
```
{% for v in variants | slice(start=1) %}
Or for {{ v.variant.id }}:

```bash
cat {{ mirror }}/{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}.toml >> ~/.config/starship.toml
```

```toml
palette = '{{ theme.id }}-{{ v.variant.id }}'
```
{% endfor %}
## How It Works

This overrides Starship's standard named colors, so your existing module configurations will automatically use {{ theme.name }} colors without any changes.

